# Emdee — line-ending policy.
#
# The repository stores text as LF and checks it out as LF on every platform,
# including Windows.  Without this file Git's `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows
# default) rewrites the working tree to CRLF, and the first tool that writes a
# file with LF turns an unrelated commit into a thousand-line whitespace diff.
# Pinning it here means a Windows checkout and a Linux checkout are byte-identical.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that must keep LF whatever a local override says: a shebang line
# ending in CR is a "bad interpreter" error, not a cosmetic problem.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.desktop text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the one exception — cmd.exe is only reliably happy
# with CRLF, and Inno Setup's compiler reads its script either way.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch the bytes, never try to diff them as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
